		{"id":"31bbee9459bcbfc8","type":"group","x":1350,"y":460,"width":1520,"height":1260,"label":"Dashboard"},
		{"id":"19fa566c73d65303","type":"group","x":240,"y":460,"width":1030,"height":1260,"label":"Backend"},
		{"id":"908580f0be857af2","type":"group","x":240,"y":2020,"width":540,"height":1040,"label":"Validation"},
		{"id":"30b03eff8906f73f","type":"group","x":240,"y":-320,"width":540,"height":440,"label":"Architecture"},
		{"id":"canvas-errors","type":"text","text":"## Errors\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-750,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"## Legend\n🔴 **Red** = To Do (ready)\n⬜ **Gray** = Blocked\n🟠 **Orange** = Doing\n🔵 **Cyan** = Ready to review\n🟢 **Green** = Done\n🟣 **Purple** = Proposed by agent","x":-540,"y":-310,"width":380,"height":230,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"canvas-warnings","type":"text","text":"## Warnings\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-530,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"5378006f2b182995","type":"text","text":"## BA-03 WebSocket server, schema, and serialization\nImplement the server transport, the bidirectional message schema, and payload serialization. Keep control/session messages lightweight and define two data tiers: low-rate process frames and oscilloscope pulse chunks.","x":300,"y":1280,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"041eb41491ffd347","type":"text","text":"## VA-01 End-to-end integration test\nVerify the live path end-to-end: session startup, frame delivery, panel rendering, command propagation within one control step, pause/resume behavior, and stable playback under bounded buffering.","x":300,"y":2060,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"5b21e739de83033a","type":"text","text":"## VA-02 Launch script and docs\nAdd a single entrypoint for launching realtime mode and document the merged architecture, supported live parameters, pacing options, and known performance limits in the project docs.","x":300,"y":2840,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"99a7fe3336c6c053","type":"text","text":"## DA-01 Live data source abstraction and websocket client\nAdd a dashboard data-source abstraction that supports both the existing file-backed flow and a live append-only flow. Include the browser WebSocket client, ring buffers, reconnect handling, and backpressure strategy.\n\nï»¿### Changes\n- Added `visualization/js/utils/dataSource.js` with a shared dashboard data-source abstraction, a file-backed source, and a live WebSocket-backed source.\n- Implemented live-source ring buffers for process frames and pulse chunks, drop-oldest backpressure, reconnect backoff, session-header/session-state handling, and a clean `send()` surface for later control messages.\n- Updated `DashboardController` to consume data through a source layer instead of assuming direct file-loaded arrays, while preserving the legacy `this.data` shape so existing panels continue to work until their live-specific tasks land.\n- Added controller hooks for `connectLiveStream()` / `disconnectLiveStream()`, timeline bound refresh from the active source, and live-tail following for incoming process frames.\n- Verification: imported the rewritten dashboard modules through a temporary `.mjs` mirror and ran a smoke check covering file source frame counts, live source ring-buffer trimming, pulse backpressure trimming, and `DashboardController` importability (`frontend smoke ok`).","x":1410,"y":500,"width":420,"height":660,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"47e851f4e4a2a67e","type":"text","text":"## DA-02 Adapt process panels for append-only data\nUpdate side view, top view, and thermal profile flows that currently assume complete preloaded arrays so they render correctly from bounded live history and incremental metadata.","x":1410,"y":1280,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"a8be8e4710ab2c3e","type":"text","text":"## DA-03 Rework oscilloscope for chunked pulse traces\nModify the oscilloscope to consume chunked voltage/current pulse history from the live buffer instead of assuming one global microsecond-indexed array. Preserve trigger behavior, rolling windows, and channel controls.","x":1900,"y":1280,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"50759d9ff8147fcb","type":"text","text":"## DA-04 Live parameter controls UI\nAdd runtime controls for the live session: servo command or setpoint, target gap or target average voltage, generator voltage, current mode, and ON/OFF timing. Send debounced updates and surface echoed applied values and connection state.","x":2390,"y":1280,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"3e82fd6c968fde66","type":"text","text":"## AR-01 Define realtime session contract\nLock the merged realtime MVP contract before coding: compiled-fast base loop, supported live-editable parameters versus restart-only parameters, process-frame versus pulse-chunk streaming, pacing semantics, and browser/server message responsibilities.\n\n### Changes\n- Added docs/realtime_mode_contract.md as the MVP contract for live mode.\n- Locked the session model, pacing semantics, and the single-WebSocket MVP transport shape.\n- Defined the live-editable parameter set versus restart-only configuration.\n- Locked the two-tier stream model: process_frame at control-step resolution and pulse_chunk for oscilloscope history.\n- Defined browser/server responsibilities and MVP non-goals so follow-on tasks can implement without reopening core scope questions.\n- Notes: docs-only task; no tests run.","x":300,"y":-280,"width":420,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"88ee9be598eb5c6c","type":"text","text":"## BA-01 Realtime runner with pacing and lifecycle\nImplement the long-lived realtime runner around the compiled-fast path. Own session lifecycle, pause/resume/stop, playback ratio pacing, and periodic state publication at control-step boundaries.\n\n### Changes\n- Added `wedm.realtime.session.RealtimeSession`, a long-lived compiled-fast runner with session lifecycle states (`created`, `running`, `paused`, `stopped`), thread-safe `pause()`, `resume()`, `stop()`, and mutable playback slowdown.\n- Added boundary publication dataclasses: `PulseChunk`, `RealtimeControlStep`, and `RealtimeSessionStatus` so downstream transport code can consume control-step snapshots without coupling to the CLI runner.\n- Reused the compiled scheduler cleanly by adding `WireEDMEnv.prime_compiled_action()` and a shared packet loader, which allows realtime sessions to preload the first action and then run fixed control intervals without the batch-runner bootstrap quirk.\n- Added safe hot-state capture via `build_hot_state_bundle(copy_arrays=True)` for control-step publication.\n- Added targeted tests covering paced control-step emission, live control updates across intervals, solver-limited fallback, and pause/resume/stop lifecycle behavior.\n- Verification: `python -m pytest SPARC/tests/test_realtime_session.py -q`; `python -m pytest SPARC/tests/test_realtime_control_state.py -q`; `python -m pytest SPARC/tests -q -k \"simulation_runner or runner\"`.","x":300,"y":500,"width":420,"height":660,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"9bf613b39c7d933b","type":"text","text":"## BA-02 Refactor closure-captured control state\nRefactor the existing controller/setpoint handling so target gap, target average voltage, fixed servo, generator voltage, current mode, and ON/OFF timing can be mutated safely while a session is running.\n\nï»¿### Changes\n- Added `wedm.realtime.control` with `RuntimeControlState`, immutable `RuntimeControlSnapshot`, and `RuntimeController` so live-adjustable setpoints/generator fields can mutate without rebuilding controller closures.\n- Refactored `experiments/simulation_runner.py` controller factories to return `RuntimeController` instances while preserving existing gap, voltage, and fixed-servo behavior for batch runs.\n- Updated verbose runner reporting to read from the runtime control snapshot instead of stale closure arguments.\n- Added targeted tests covering hot updates for gap, voltage, and fixed-servo modes plus rejection of inactive or restart-only parameters.\n- Verification: `python -m pytest SPARC/tests/test_realtime_control_state.py -q`; `python -m pytest SPARC/tests -q -k \"simulation_runner or runner\"`.","x":760,"y":500,"width":420,"height":660,"color":"5"}
	],
